libwebrtc
---------

A build with calls (district-call's `livekit` feature, which the app's `voice`
feature turns on) statically links libwebrtc as LiveKit prebuilds it for its Rust
SDK: release webrtc-89d790b of github.com/livekit/rust-sdks, the file
webrtc-linux-x64-release.zip, SHA-256
b167adad5291cea0e4d66a0454d9d52d2ad714e6b0ed70f4410317d3ebde70c5, which is the
pin in scripts/fetch-libwebrtc.sh. The archive's LICENSE.md, which that script
unpacks beside the library, holds the full licence text of every component
below, and a distribution of such a build must ship it with the binary. The
default build links none of this.

