FFmpeg: the archive builds FFmpeg's H.264 and H.265 decoders into the library,
and they are linked into a build with calls, as are the H.264, AV1, VP8 and VP9
codecs above, although the app sends and receives no video. LICENSE.md's FFmpeg
entry holds the texts of the GNU General Public License versions 2 and 3 and the
GNU Lesser General Public License versions 2.1 and 3, and does not say which of
them applies to the code linked. No build with calls has been distributed, and
none should be until that, and the patent licensing of the H.264 and H.265
decoders, has been reviewed. A libwebrtc built without them would remove the
question.

